### Post-Gate Deployment and Production Validation Checkpoint

After all three gates pass for every sprint story, the lead MUST:
1. Run sprint-level review (adversarial + party mode on complete sprint)
2. Build and deploy to production: `{deploy_command}`
   <!-- {deploy_command}: Your project's build and deploy command -->
3. Run live smoke tests: `{smoke_test_command}`
   <!-- {smoke_test_command}: Your project's live smoke test command -->
4. Verify the deployed build contains the expected changes
5. Present the **Production Validation Checkpoint** to the human:
   - Summary of what was built and deployed
   - Link to gate log (`_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/gate-log.md`)
   - Link to escalation log (`docs/escalations/pending.md`) -- highlight
     any `DECIDED_AUTONOMOUSLY` or `DEFERRAL_REQUEST` entries
   - Confirmation that smoke tests passed
   - For UI sprints: confirm deployed UI renders correctly with production data

This is the **only human checkpoint** in the AI/DLC pipeline. The human
reviews the deployed production instance, the gate log, and any autonomous
decisions. For multi-sprint features (Rule 9), this checkpoint occurs after
each sprint -- the agent does not proceed to the next sprint until the human
validates the current one.

This applies to every sprint, not just UI work. Never ask the human to
deploy. Never report "ready for review" without having already deployed
and validated the running production instance.

### Shutdown Protocol

- Lead requests shutdown from all teammates before cleanup.
- Teammates approve shutdown (confirming no in-progress work will be lost).
- Lead runs cleanup only after all teammates have exited.

